<title>USA: Eclipse angina treatment called &quot;promising&quot;.</title>
<headline>Eclipse angina treatment called &quot;promising&quot;.</headline>
<dateline>SUNNYVALE, Calif. 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Eclipse Surgical Technologies Inc, said Friday that it had &quot;promising&quot; follow-up results in its randomized Phase II clinical trial of Transmyocardial Revascularization (TMR), a treatment for patients with angina and severe heart disease.</p>
<p>The company said the data will form the basis of its pre-market approval application to the Food and Drug Administration later this summer, after asix month follow-up is completed.</p>
<p>Eclipse is a medical device company specializing in cardiac revascularization products for the treatment of advanced cardiovascular disease.</p>
